---
description: agent-docs — track multi-step tasks as living context docs
alwaysApply: true
---

At the START of any task with more than one step, read and follow the agent-docs
skill only when every project/work target resolves inside `/Users/manzanita/Repositories/`:

    /Users/manzanita/Repositories/dog-code/docs/agent-docs/dev/agent-docs-skill.md

If any target resolves outside `/Users/manzanita/Repositories/`, including
`~/personal_code`, do not create or update anything in
`/Users/manzanita/Repositories/dog-code/docs/agent-docs/`.

Create/update a living context doc under `/Users/manzanita/Repositories/dog-code/docs/agent-docs/` (one doc
per task, registered in the index, phases + per-phase model tags). These docs live
in `dog-code`, so the developer commits and pushes them; the agent must not perform
state-changing Git operations for them. The same restriction applies to
`craftlog-js-api`. In every other workspace repository, scoped Git operations,
including commit and push, are allowed when they are a normal part of the requested work.
